Rejection of interviewed candidates
When a candidate has been advanced into conversations and the decision has been made to not move forward with a candidate, a timely, personal rejection should be sent to the candidate. A candidate that we interview has spent an enormous time with Oxide: not only have they done their candidate materials, they have also been into the RFDs, prepared for conversations, had many conversations, etc.; such candidates are owed our prompt candor.